From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:07:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: Use the AARCH64_4K page table format on the
 Exynos9820

The Mali-G76 MP12 (r0p0) in the Exynos9820 is not IO coherent.  In the
legacy (LPAE) page table mode every buffer is mapped outer write-allocate
and outer shareable, and the table walker gets no memory attributes at
all.  Busy multi-context clients (KWin and plasmashell) then hit a steady
stream of job faults (DATA_INVALID_FAULT, IMPRECISE_FAULT, JOB_BUS_FAULT,
INSTR_INVALID_ENC) and visible corruption, with the descriptor the job
chain points at reading back as zeros.  Simple single-context programs
run clean, and several Mesa releases behave the same, so this is not a
userspace regression.

The vendor kernel (Mali kbase bv_r32p1 in the Galaxy S10 sources) only
ever runs this GPU with AARCH64_4K tables, and the Mali-G57 in the
MT8188 needed the same switch for the same class of faults.  Match the
SoC compatible and force that format.

Measured on a Galaxy S10+: 202 job faults in the first 165 s after boot
with the legacy format, none in 325 s with this change, including a
full-CPU load and 1080p60 video playback.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c
index 784e36d72c2..08790c84d92 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c
@@ -1078,6 +1078,19 @@ static const struct panfrost_compatible default_data = {
 	.pm_domain_names = NULL,
 };
 
+/*
+ * The Mali-G76 in the Exynos9820 is not IO coherent and faults at random in
+ * the legacy page table mode, like the Mali-G57 in the MT8188: jobs from
+ * busy multi-context clients read back descriptors as zeros.  The vendor
+ * kernel only ever runs it with AARCH64_4K tables.
+ */
+static const struct panfrost_compatible exynos9820_data = {
+	.num_supplies = ARRAY_SIZE(default_supplies) - 1,
+	.supply_names = default_supplies,
+	.num_pm_domains = 1, /* optional */
+	.gpu_quirks = BIT(GPU_QUIRK_FORCE_AARCH64_PGTABLE),
+};
+
 static const struct panfrost_compatible default_pm_rt_data = {
 	.num_supplies = ARRAY_SIZE(default_supplies) - 1,
 	.supply_names = default_supplies,
@@ -1178,6 +1191,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id dt_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt8192-mali", .data = &mediatek_mt8192_data },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt8370-mali", .data = &mediatek_mt8370_data },
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-mali", .data = &default_pm_rt_data },
+	{ .compatible = "samsung,exynos9820-mali", .data = &exynos9820_data },
 	{}
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, dt_match);
